  "decision_conditions": [
    "Condition : 1 - The development hereby permitted must be begun not later than the end of three years from the date of this permission.\r\n\r\nReason: In order to comply with the provisions of Section 91 of the Town and Country Planning Act 1990 (as amended).\r\n\r\n",
    "Condition : 2 - The development hereby permitted shall be carried out in accordance with the following approved plans \r\n\r\nHunters Lodge- Supporting Design and Heritage Statement Feb 2026, Burghley_3m_Cedar_Summerhouse Proposed Elevations and Plans, 6018-003 Proposed block plan, 6018-002-B Hunters Lodge - Existing Site Block Plan, 6018-004 Existing Plan and Elevations, Method_Statement_Dec2025-Tree Protection_Hunters Lodge-RevA, 6018-001-Hunters Lodge - Site Location Plan.\r\n\r\nReason: For the avoidance of doubt and in the interest of proper planning.\r\n",
    "Condition : 3 - Prior to the commencement of works on site, tree protection measures shall be installed and working practices adopted in accordance with the document entitled Supporting Design & Heritage Statement Revision A\" received 11/02/2026 by Clear Future Architecture and document entitled 'Impact Assessment, Method Statement for Protection of Trees and Tree Protection Plan'. received 10/12/2026 by Clear Future Architecture. All trees on the site, or parts of trees grow from adjoining sites, unless shown on the permitted drawings as being removed, shall be retained and protected from damage in accordance with BS5837:2012 and with the approved protection details. The development shall be monitored by the project arboriculturalist in accordance with the approved report. \r\n\r\nReason: To ensure that the development will not have an adverse effect on existing trees and in order to maintain the character and amenity of the area in accordance with the requirements of policies A2 and A3 of the Camden Local Plan.",
    "Condition : 4 - The development hereby approved shall only be used for purposes incidental to the dwellinghouse (5 Belsize Lane) and not for any non-residential/non domestic purposes. \r\n\r\nReason:  To protect the amenity of neighbouring occupiers and the character of the area in accordance with policies A1, D1 and D2 of the Camden Local Plan 2017."
  ],
